    "propInertiaSource": "Propeller + spinner + the crank's rotating parts, kg.m2. From the OWNER'S BLADE RULE (2026-11-09, tools/aircraft_builder/prop_inertia.py): each blade is 15 % of the net propeller weight with its centre of mass at 25 % of the DIAMETER from the axis, the rest being hub near the axis - because a heavy constant-speed hub contributes almost nothing to sum(m r^2), so a mass-weighted estimate overstates the couple. M 17.5 kg, D 1.93 m, 2 blades: blades 1.222 + hub 0.123 (k 0.10 m) + crank 0.07 = 1.41, against 1.7 before. MASS: ESTIMATED: Sensenich 76EM8 forged aluminium fixed-pitch, ~38 lb. O-360, four cylinders. VALIDATION: the rule reproduces Hartzell's published two-blade polar moment to +18 % (1.412 against 1.198) and runs +60 % high on their three-blade one, so it is applied to two-blade types only.",
